---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import CodesPage from '../components/v2/templates/CodesPage.astro';
import { siteImages } from '../data/images';
import { getPageSEO } from '../utils/seo';

const faqItems = [
  { question: 'Which Karinderya codes are currently listed by the developer?', answer: 'The official Roblox game description listed DECOPART1, BRGYPERMIT, and 100KCCU when this page was reviewed on September 9, 2026. A listing does not guarantee that a code can still be redeemed on every account.' },
  { question: 'Why is a Karinderya code not accepted?', answer: 'Check for typing errors and extra spaces, then consider whether the account has already redeemed it or the server has a newer code state.' },
  { question: 'Where are Karinderya codes entered?', answer: 'Use the code control shown by the current game interface. If it is not visible, finish the opening prompts before checking again.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout pageId="codes" breadcrumbs={[{label:'Home',href:'/'},{label:getPageSEO('codes').h1}]}>
<CodesPage
  title={getPageSEO('codes').h1}
  kicker="Code help"
  intro="The official Karinderya Roblox page currently lists DECOPART1, BRGYPERMIT, and 100KCCU. Reward details are not confirmed here."
  relatedLinks={[
    { label: 'Beginner Guide', href: '/guides/beginner-guide/' },
    { label: 'Updates', href: '/updates/' },
    { label: 'Guides', href: '/guides/' },
  ]}
  tableOfContents
  heroImage={siteImages.codesHero}
>
  <h2 id="direct-answer">Direct Answer</h2>
  <p>When this page was reviewed on September 9, 2026, the official Roblox game description listed <code>DECOPART1</code>, <code>BRGYPERMIT</code>, and <code>100KCCU</code>. This confirms that the developer currently publishes these strings, but it does not prove that every code is redeemable on every account or server.</p>

  <h2 id="officially-listed-codes">Current Officially Listed Codes</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Public classification</th><th>Reward</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>DECOPART1</code></td><td>Listed in the official Roblox description</td><td>Reward details are not confirmed.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>BRGYPERMIT</code></td><td>Listed in the official Roblox description</td><td>Reward details are not confirmed.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>100KCCU</code></td><td>Listed in the official Roblox description</td><td>Reward details are not confirmed.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>

  <h2 id="historical-codes">Historical Codes</h2>
  <p><code>50KCCU</code>, <code>2MVISITS</code>, <code>3MVISITS</code>, and <code>BATINATAYOHA</code> appear in dated community redemption records. They are not listed in the current official Roblox description, so this Wiki does not present them as current codes. Historical reports also differ on parts of some rewards.</p>

  <h2 id="how-to-use-codes">How to Redeem Codes</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open Karinderya and finish any opening prompts that hide the regular interface.</li>
    <li>Open the current code control and enter only the code string.</li>
    <li>Remove spaces before or after the text.</li>
    <li>Submit the entry once and read the message displayed by the game.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="troubleshooting">Why a Code May Not Work</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Check every character and match capitalization.</li>
    <li>Make sure no extra spaces were included.</li>
    <li>Consider whether the account has already used the same code.</li>
    <li>Rejoin an updated server if the game has recently changed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="verification-method">How This Page Is Checked</h2>
  <p>Current code strings are taken from the public description of the official Roblox experience. Exact rewards are published only when creator-owned information or a recent, reviewable redemption record supports them. The current server response remains the final result for an individual account.</p>

  <FAQ items={faqItems} />
</CodesPage>
</BaseLayout>
